// endpoint_set_workspace_one_shot.proto — SetWorkspaceOneShot: mark a
// workspace a one-shot after its creation, or unmark it. AGENT API section.
//
// A ONE-SHOT LANDS ITSELF WHEN ITS WORK IS DONE. A workspace created as one is
// told so in its first message (the repository's completion directive); an
// ordinary workspace whose agent commits to finishing the rest of its work
// unattended marks itself one here, and the answer carries the same
// directive, so a workspace that became a one-shot is told exactly what one
// created as one was told. The mark is what every surface draws a one-shot
// from (the roster's one-shot mark, WorkspaceStatus.one_shot); the daemon
// performs nothing on the agent's behalf: the agent carries the directive
// out.
//
// A CHILD ITS OWNER LANDS IS NEVER A ONE-SHOT: landing it is its owner's act,
// so marking one is refused (`owner_lands`), as creating one is
// (CreateWorkspaceError.one_shot_owner_lands).

